{"name":"Nosegay","hex":"#ffe6ec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nosegay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small bunch of fragrant flowers or herbs tied in a bundle, often presented as a gift; nosegays were originally intended to be put to the nose for the pleasant sensation or to mask unpleasant odours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An aroma, a scent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nosegay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nosegay","blocks":[{"text":"A nosegay, posy, or tussie-mussie is a small flower bouquet. They have existed in some form since at least medieval times, when they were carried or worn around the head or bodice. Doilies are traditionally used to bind the stems in these arrangements. Alternatively, \"posy holders\", available in a variety of shapes and materials, enable the wearing of these arrangements \"at the waist, in the hair, or secured with a brooch\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_nosegay_LCCN2002710681.jpg/330px-The_nosegay_LCCN2002710681.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nosegay","wikidata":"Q14125324"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg/500px-Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg/1280px-Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg/500px-Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bouquet holder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHolder%2C_bouquet_(AM_67821-8).jpg"}],"sounds":{"nosegay":[{"type":"audio/flac","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/En-us-nosegay.flac?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/En-us-nosegay.flac/En-us-nosegay.flac.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/En-us-nosegay.flac/En-us-nosegay.flac.ogg"}]}}}